  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "sUf/8jCHuJwnGuJkHxEhMWNexxE=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:14.727Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "a16z crypto's core economic claim: when execution becomes cheap through AI, **verification becomes the scarce resource**. Blockchains, onchain attestations, and decentralized identity systems shift the economic boundary of safe agent deployment by providing clear, auditable history instead of treating AI as a black box.\n\n**Why it matters:** the bottleneck in agent adoption is not capability but the counterparty question \u2014 *can this agent be trusted with money and authority?* Systems that make agent behavior verifiable capture the value that trust intermediaries capture today.\n\n**Converging claim:** Microsoft researchers independently frame the agentic economy as one where \"trust, not attention, is the scarce resource.\"\n\nSource: a16z crypto, \"5 Ways Blockchains Can Help AI Agents\" (https://a16zcrypto.com/posts/article/5-ways-blockchains-help-ai-agents/).",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-30T12:10:00.000Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-30T18:30:14.727Z"
    }
  },
